Drag the caret by pressing on it, and keep the magnifier below the shell bar.

On a phone people press the caret itself and drag it, as in any HarmonyOS
text field. Chromium only takes the handle below it, and touches on the
text line above the handle deliberately fall through. On OHOS:

- For the insertion handle only, a touch on the caret line within a touch
  radius counts as a touch on the handle: pressing the caret and dragging
  moves it, tapping it toggles the menu. Selection handles are unchanged.
- After typing, handles are off and TouchSelectionController dropped the
  caret's bounds, so the first press on the caret selected a word and only
  the second moved it. The caret's bounds are kept while handles are off,
  and a press on the caret brings the insertion handle back and gives it
  the touch.
- The magnifier sits above the caret and is kept inside its parent layer,
  the root window's, whose top is under the shell's status and address
  bars. It is now parented to a transparent layer in the root layer that
  covers only the visible page, so it stays below the bars and its backdrop
  zoom still sees the page. (Parented to the page's own layer, as the first
  version of this patch did, it saw nothing and drew opaque.)

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 with chromium-154-harmonyos.patch
and ohos-touch-menu-below-shell-bar.patch applied. Apply with:
  git apply ohos-touch-caret-drag.patch

